# Task Status Table protocol

On **every multi-step task**, show an indexed status table **in the chat response** (never only a canvas).

## Status icons

| Icon | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| 🟢 | Done |
| 🔴 | Left / still to do |
| 🟡 | Deliberately waiting on something else first |

## Before work

1. Show the planned work as a numbered markdown table **before** making changes.
2. Mark planned items 🔴 (or 🟡 if blocked on an external dependency).
3. Pause so Arham can verify scope. If he already said "go", proceed after showing the table.

Example:

| # | Item | Status | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | … | 🔴 | … |
| 2 | … | 🟡 | blocked on X |
| 3 | … | 🟢 | already done |

## After work

1. Show the **same indexed table** updated.
2. Unchanged 🟢 stays 🟢 (no arrow).
3. Status changes use transition arrows: `🔴 → 🟢`, `🟡 → 🟢`, `🔴 → 🟡`, etc.
4. Leftover work stays 🔴 or 🟡.

Example:

| # | Item | Status | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | … | 🔴 → 🟢 | … |
| 2 | … | 🟡 | still waiting on X |
| 3 | … | 🟢 | unchanged |

## Rules of thumb

- Put the table **in chat** with emoji so **reds are easy to scan**.
- One row per concrete deliverable, not vague phases.
- Do not invent fake greens — if not done, keep 🔴/🟡.
- Skip the table for trivial one-liner asks (e.g. "what is X?").
